\fs6 \

\pard\f0\b0\fs28\fi-620\li2520\fc0\cf0 + (NSArray *)
\b imageFileTypes
\b0  \

\fs14 \

\pard\tx3600\tx3980\tx4340\fs28\li1500\fc0\cf0 Returns an array of strings representing those file types for which a registered NSImageRep exists. This list includes all file types supported by registered subclasses of NSImageRep, plus those types that can be converted to supported file types through a user-installed filter service. The array returned by this method may be passed directly to the NSOpenPanel's 
\b runModalForTypes:
\b0  method.\

\fs14 \

\fs28 File types are identified by extension. By default, the list returned by this method contains ªtiffº, ªtifº, ªbmpº, and ªepsº.\

\fs14 \

\fs28 When creating a subclass of NSImageRep that accepts image data from non-default file types, override NSImageRep's 
\b imageUnfilteredFileTypes
\b0  method to notify NSImage of the file types your class supports. \

\fs14 \

